        "text": "At its core, a blockchain is a special type of database, sometimes referred to as a distributed ledger. Blockchains are one of the most common types of distributed ledger technology systems, so both terms are often used interchangeably. Keep in mind, however, that not all distributed ledger technology systems are blockchains. A blockchain stores information, just like a spreadsheet, but the information is subject to special rules. The rules are 1. Data can be added 2. Data cannot be removed or modified 3 each piece of data must point back to the previous piece.",
